  "id": "DrugBank_DB14031 - MONDO_16096",
  "verbalization": "Tretamine appears to have a potential role in the treatment of Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, based on its association with similar tumors through the indicated pathways. The evidence suggests that Tretamine may act as a therapeutic agent for tumors of the ovary that are not classified as dysgerminomatous, as it is linked to Altretamine, which is known to target similar tumors. The shared indication with Altretamine implies a possible mechanism of action that is relevant to both types of germ cell tumors. The presence of a direct indication from Tretamine to the target tumor type, along with the indirect pathway through Altretamine, supports the hypothesis that Tretamine may exert a biological effect on these tumors. The mechanism of action is likely related to the inhibition of tumor growth or suppression of malignant cell proliferation, as indicated by the presence of a known therapeutic agent (Altretamine) in the same pathway. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Tretamine and the disease, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and therapeutic potential.",
